+# 25 — Samus charge/shot: correct overlap with the arm cannon
+
+**Version:** runtime-candidate research revision, 2026-09-14.
+**Inspected base:** `a5c5bc08d8e8661658865216798d600462db948e` (`master`).
+**Priority / scope:** Attack attachment / local occlusion.
+**Existing owner:** Samus effect/weapon owner + shared depth owner.
+**Status:** OPEN — candidate code/proposals, not a ROM-verified fix.
+
+Read [COMMON.md](COMMON.md). Reconcile the actual working tree, source-derived
+assets and current board before changing code. Preserve unrelated edits.
+
+## Owner report (preserved)
+
+> B charge/shots are not rendering over the samus gun, can move Z depth to be infront of gun so that the gun is occluded when charging.
+
+## Current source findings
+
+The shared item route deliberately re-enables G_ZBUFFER; link-14 weapon display intentionally clears it. The charge effect and detached shot may have different owners and depth contracts. The user’s suggested Z movement is an option to evaluate, not proof of a wrong source attachment.
+
+Source keys: [R75](research/SOURCE_LEDGER.md#r75), [R76](research/SOURCE_LEDGER.md#r76), [R78](research/SOURCE_LEDGER.md#r78), [R105](research/SOURCE_LEDGER.md#r105).
+These distinguish directly inspected code from repository-recorded proof; none
+is a new ROM run by this package's author.
+
+## Potential runtime fix
+
+Identify charging orb versus launched shot owner/link and compare source attachment/joint matrix and size. For a source no-Z overlay, preserve that presentation using the existing native painter route after the cannon; for a source-Z model, use actual source-projected depth and correct joint placement. Audit the effect case with R02 separately. Fix mistaken weapon/effect classification or copied transform before introducing any camera-facing bias. A bounded source-derived bias is a last candidate only when exact placement is correct and the DS mapping demonstrably loses intended coverage.
+
+### Executable candidate diffs
+
+[R02_effect_initial_z.patch](runtime/R02_effect_initial_z.patch) — **CONDITIONAL CANDIDATE / sibling audit required**.
+
+Check preimages with `python Briefs/tools/check_candidates.py --repo . --candidate R02`. Applying a patch and passing a host test do not establish natural-path correctness.
+
+Implementation contract and code-oriented integration details: [research/MATERIAL_DEPTH_AND_STAGE_REPAIRS.md](research/MATERIAL_DEPTH_AND_STAGE_REPAIRS.md).
+
+## Disprove this candidate before stacking patches
+
+Do not globally pull all Samus shots toward the camera: that can break stage/fighter occlusion after launch. Test several camera angles, scales, charge sizes and both facings.
+
+## Acceptance for this symptom
+
+The charge and emerging shot occlude the intended arm-cannon region while retaining correct world depth against the rest of Samus, other fighters and stage geometry. Beginning/full-charge/release and both facings pass. Preserve projectile origin/gameplay and source animation; document any justified visual delta rather than hiding it.
+
+## Required regression scope
+
+Impact-wave rear/front occlusion, shields/reflector, other attached effects, Samus morph/Catch and simultaneous projectiles.
+
+## Coordination
+
+Coordinate shared depth changes with the impact-wave brief; the two desired overlap behaviors are not identical.
+
+## Closure
+
+Apply COMMON.md's natural-path, positive-engagement, source/pixel/audio, resource,
+native-only, cadence and widest-relevant-verifier requirements. Record candidate
